    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so `customerCode` is now `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, dropping sequence numbers entirely.\n\n**Change** (in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`): replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` \u2014 which built the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` per-city sequence \u2014 with a new `customerCode(owner)` method:\n\n- **REGION** = `owner.getLocality()`, the region derivation shared with locality (postcode range first \u2014 NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099 \u2014 falling back to the city, or `UNKNOWN`).\n- **HASH8** = first 8 upper-case hex characters of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName` (telephone already normalized to E.164 at that point), via a new `sha256UpperHex` helper.\n\n**Downstream values moved automatically** because they already read from `customerCode`:\n- `getMembershipNumber()` \u2192 `<REGION>-<HASH8>-M<YY>`\n- `getCheckDigit()` \u2192 Luhn over the digits of the new code\n- The create audit line \u2192 logs the new region-and-hash `customerCode`\n\nI also refreshed the now-stale javadoc example in `Owner.getMembershipNumber()` (`NSW-1A2B3C4D-M26`). Locality derivation itself is unchanged, as the tests (Cp17, Cp30) require. All 45 tests pass.",
